 -- SSH VPN GUI Maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:35:26 +0300

ssh-vpn-gui (0.2.36) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on polkitd and pkexec instead of the policykit-1 transitional
    package, which Ubuntu 26.04 no longer ships. Drop the hard sudo
    dependency (pkexec is the default path) and add iputils-ping, which
    the tunnel watchdog needs.
  * Kill switch without a gap: every route into the tunnel now has a
    blackhole route behind it, so when ssh dies the kernel drops
    tunneled traffic at once instead of sending it out the WAN until
    the app notices. Works with the window closed.
  * Per-IP proxy routes learned from DNS get the same blackhole, so an
    app that caches an address past its DNS TTL stays blocked too.
  * Reconnecting from the blocked state keeps the block until the new
    tunnel is routed, keeps the SSH server reachable (also a newly
    selected one, and after a network change), and no longer fails in
    full-tunnel mode. Mode switches and rule reloads add the new routes
    before removing the old ones; the nftables table is swapped in one
    transaction.
  * Reject outgoing IPv6 in full-tunnel mode as well.
  * Open in the blocked state when the tunnel died while the window was
    closed.

